From: CloudBook Air Linux Port <port@cloudbookair.local>
Subject: [PATCH] mt76: mt7663s: enable firmware TX A-MPDU/RA on 2.4/5 GHz and optimize SDIO TX/RX

Enable hardware/firmware TX A-MPDU aggregation and firmware rate control
on MT7663S (W103D / V3 N9 firmware) across both 2.4 GHz and 5 GHz while
optimizing SDIO TX/RX quota polling:

1. SDIO TX/RX path (mt7663s_txrx.c, mt7663s_w103d.h, mt7663s_w103d.c):
   - Increase W103D_TX_WORKER_ROUNDS from 8 to 16, tighten backoff to
     usleep_range(50, 100), reduce W103D_QUOTA_WATCHDOG_MS to 1 ms, and
     raise W103D_TX_QUOTA_RETRY_MAX to 4.
   - Replace word-by-word WTQCR reads with a 20-byte sdio_memcpy_fromio()
     burst and simplify tx_quota_empty().

2. Firmware RA & TX A-MPDU for unicast QoS data (mt7663s_w103d.c):
   - Clear MT_TXD2_FIX_RATE and MT_TXD2_BA_DISABLE and zero txwi[6] for
     unicast QoS data (excluding USE_MINRATE control/EAPOL frames) on both
     5 GHz and 2.4 GHz so N9 firmware RA and hardware A-MPDU own TX.
   - Sync connected BSS/STA state to N9 on association and bandwidth change
     in gen4m order (CMD 0x12 UPDATE_BSS_INFO conn_state=0 -> CMD 0x19
     BSS_RLM -> CMD 0x13 STA_STATE_3) with RCU-safe record construction.

3. Online scan & hot-reload stability (mt7663s_w103d.c):
   - Transition N9 BSS 0 transiently to conn_state=1 in hw_scan(), drop
     unbalanced MCU_EVENT_BSS_ABSENCE (0x11) events (which V3 firmware
     emits with is_absent=1 on scan without a matching resume), wake TX
     queues on SCAN_DONE/disconnect, and re-acquire 5 GHz channel
     privilege + connected BSS/STA state via scan_restore_work.
   - Guard wiphy->reg_notifier until mcu_ops and MT76_STATE_MCU_RUNNING
     are ready so rmmod/modprobe with a cached country regdomain cannot
     dereference NULL mcu_ops.
